// An environment variable absent from the sandbox fixture reads as `none`, not a failure —
// optional configuration is ordinary data, so `??` supplies the default. Identical in both
// backends. (Contrast `fs.read` on a missing file, which is still an E0021: a program that
// names a file means it; a program that reads `env` usually has a fallback in mind.)
// expect: stdout "fallback"
// expect: stdout "true"
// expect: exit 0
use std.{env};

echo env.get("DOES_NOT_EXIST") ?? "fallback";
echo env.get("DOES_NOT_EXIST") == none;
